examples/**/*.png

# Internal research outputs (not for distribution)
#
# Anchored with a leading slash: these name directories at the REPO ROOT.
# Unanchored, `profiling/` also matched `src/tengri/profiling/` -- a real,
# tracked package -- and ruff respects .gitignore inside a git repository, so
# CI silently linted 1464 files instead of 1468 and those four were invisible
# to `ruff check`. Two defects sat in them unreported (#1598). Keep the slash;
# `explore/` had the same latent hazard and is anchored for the same reason.
analysis/figures/
/explore/
/profiling/
notebook_execution.log
notebook_metrics.json
# Per-notebook nbconvert transcripts (`=== Running NN (timeout 1800s) ===` plus
# XLA warnings). `notebook_execution.log` above covers the single combined log;
# these are the per-notebook ones the orchestrator writes alongside it.
notebooks/logs/

# Sphinx docs build artifacts
docs/_build/
docs/_notebooks/
docs/build.log
# docs/auto_examples/ is committed (pre-rendered locally) so the docs build
# in CI doesn't need SSP grids or RELAGN — see docs/conf.py plot_gallery.
# Re-run `make html` locally and commit changes when galleries need refresh.
# docs/auto_examples/
.worktrees/
.claude/
.nb_home/

# Notebook runtime data caches (SVO filter pulls, etc.)
notebooks/data/
examples/*/data/filters/
# Contents, not the directory itself. Git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded -- it never descends far enough to see the negation --
# so `examples/*/data/` would make the exception below silently inert.
examples/*/data/**
# The one committed input under that tree: an example reads this NED SED, so it
# is not a cache. Eight filter curves under notebooks/data/filters/ were tracked
# the same way -- byte-identical copies of data/filters/, deleted rather than
# re-included, for the reason the twenty under examples/ were (#1857).
!examples/dust_attenuation/data/haro11_ned_sed.txt
arxiv_library/
_galrun/

# Superpowers subagent-driven-development scratch ledger (session-local)
.superpowers/

# Audit/scratch scripts must live in tests/ — never the repo root. Tests are
# collected from tests/ only (pyproject testpaths=["tests"]), so a root-level
# test_*.py is unreachable dead weight. Ignoring them here stops a `git add -A`
# from re-leaking audit scratch, as happened in #1165 (see #1232).
/test_*.py
/*_test.py
/audit_*.py
/*_audit.py
/quick_test*.py
/final_audit*.py
# Diagnostic scripts belong in scripts/diagnose/. Eight `diagnose_*.py` sat at the
# repo root until #1783 moved them; this rule is what stops the next one landing
# there, the same way the audit rules above do.
/diagnose_*.py
/_scratch*

# Stray output directories at the repo root.
#
# The spine notebooks in `notebooks/` savefig to a *relative* `_figs/`, so running
# one from the repo root writes a second, divergent copy of the same figures to
# `/_figs/` instead of `notebooks/_figs/`. That copy was tracked and had drifted a
# month stale before anyone noticed, because nothing resolves to it — the notebooks
# read `notebooks/_figs/` and the published docs read `docs/spine/_figs/`.
# `/results/` and `/figures/` accumulated single files the same way.
/_figs/
/results/
/figures/
!data/grahsp/grahsp_templates.h5
# `!data/qsogen_emline_template.h5` was here. QSOGen loads the *.dat* template
# (`find_data("qsogen_emline_template.dat")` in components/agn/qsogen.py); the
# .h5 arrived in the #1029 data-gating sweep and nothing ever read it. This
# un-ignore line was its only mention in the tree, which is what kept a 157 KB
# binary committed for a loader that wants a different file.
!data/qsogen_detailed_reference.npz
!data/external_sed_reference.npz
!data/feltre_grid.h5
!data/mappings_templates.h5
!data/schreiber2018_templates.h5
!data/bpss_stars_c3k_a_chabrier.h5
!data/flury2024_grids.h5
# ── The rest of the tracked data/, which these rules had never re-included ──
#
# Every file below was committed on purpose and is read at runtime or by the
# crossvals, yet `data/*.h5` and `*.npz` above matched all of them and nothing
# negated it. Git only applies ignore rules to *untracked* files, so they
# survived on the accident of having been added before the rule -- delete and
# re-add one, or regenerate the tree, and `git add -A` silently drops it. The
# nested data/.gitignore already carried the intent as a prose comment
# ("cue_weights.npz is tracked ... the Cue backend needs it out of the box")
# without ever expressing it as a rule, which is the same gap written down.
#
# `tools/check_tracked_not_ignored.py` now fails on any tracked file its own
# .gitignore would exclude, so this list cannot silently fall behind again.
!data/agnfitter_cold_dust_reference.h5
!data/agnfitter_torus_reference.h5
!data/astrodust_templates.h5
!data/bosa_templates.h5
!data/cigale_radio_reference.npz
!data/cigale_themis_reference.npz
!data/cue_reference_outputs.npz
!data/cue_weights.npz
!data/dale2014_templates.h5
!data/dale2014_templates_cigale.h5
!data/dl07_templates_v2.h5
!data/dl14_templates.h5
!data/fsps_mass_remaining_chabrier.h5
!data/fsps_nebular_reference.npz
!data/fsps_spectrum_reference.npz
!data/qsogen_cont_bb_only.npz
!data/qsogen_lines_reference.npz
!data/qsogen_manual_cont_bb.npz
!data/qsogen_reference.npz
!data/schreiber2016_templates.h5
!data/skirtor_templates_v2.h5
!data/themis_templates.h5

